From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:16:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 322/342] arp: a host that talks is no longer kept rejected

A request that fails marks the address rejected for ARP_REJECT_TIMEOUT
(20 s). But anything learned about the host from the network restarted
the entry's timer as the stale one (30 minutes) and kept it rejected, and
each ARP packet from the host did it again: a host that kept talking to
us stayed unreachable for good. On a C2 on Wi-Fi on 2026-11-06, after a
short outage, the SMB server, the router and the laptop all sat rejected
with Wi-Fi working; deleting the entries by hand (arp -d) brought each
back at once. Now what the network tells us about a host ends its
rejection; static entries are left as they are, and a rejected address
nobody hears from still goes after 20 s.

tools/arp-learning-test.py on the test board: "failed address that
talks" stayed rejected on +330, valid now; 9 of 9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
index 2b14303e18..2c23db0515 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/datalink_protocols/arp/arp.cpp
@@ -410,6 +410,14 @@ arp_update_entry(in_addr_t protocolAddress, sockaddr_dl *hardwareAddress,
 
 	delete_request_buffer(entry);
 
+	if (learned && (entry->flags & ARP_FLAG_PERMANENT) == 0) {
+		// A request that failed rejects the address for ARP_REJECT_TIMEOUT,
+		// but the host has just told us where it is. Kept rejected, the stale
+		// timer below would hold it for good while the host keeps talking to
+		// us: after a short outage, a server or a gateway stayed unreachable.
+		entry->flags &= ~ARP_FLAG_REJECT;
+	}
+
 	if ((entry->flags & ARP_FLAG_PERMANENT) == 0) {
 		// (re)start the stale timer
 		entry->timer_state = ARP_STATE_STALE;
